PATCH 545: the three siblings of the case patch 514 fixed -- a19e's state-change table has FOUR
entries and only one of them had been corrected.

`FUN_0000_a19e` (patch 283) is the per-object-type STATE-CHANGE dispatch: asm 0xa19e is
`mov bx,[di] ; shl bx,1 ; call [bx-0x69a2]`, i.e. word[DGROUP:0x965e + type*2], called with DI live and
passed by the port as the object HOST POINTER (one argument).

Dumped from the image at offset 0x2565e, the table has exactly four valid entries -- everything past
type 3 is ASCII data, so this is the "vehicle family" dispatch:

    type 00 -> 7da5     type 01 -> 8679     type 02 -> 8f3a     type 03 -> 96cb

All four are the same three-instruction shape, differing only in the second byte offset:

    7da5: mov %al,0x90(%di) ; movb $0x3,0xd6(%di) ; lcall 0f69:0x7a5b   (= linear 0x110EB = 70eb)
    8679: mov %al,0x90(%di) ; movb $0x3,0xc8(%di) ; lcall 0f69:0x7a5b
    8f3a: mov %al,0x90(%di) ; movb $0x3,0xca(%di) ; lcall 0f69:0x7a5b   <- fixed by patch 514
    96cb: mov %al,0x90(%di) ; movb $0x3,0xd2(%di) ; lcall 0f69:0x7a5b

Patch 514 established the convention for 8f3a and left its three siblings pristine: the object is
param_1 (a19e's host pointer), param_2 is UNINITIALISED STACK, and AL -- the gear-direction selector
ad3b sets, dropped through a19e's 1-param signature -- is published as g_fist_a19e_al.  The three
untouched functions dereferenced param_2, measured as 32165, which is a SIGSEGV the moment their state
is entered.  Their `mov al,1 ; jmp` thunks carried the same defect and are fixed with them.

This is a hard prerequisite for the extender op-0x1c ground clamp (board:0021): with op 0x1c wired up
the engine reaches this state and crashed in 7da5 (ad2f -> ad3b -> a19e -> 7da5) until this patch.

Measured, no regression on its own: AZER1 a296 12 (unchanged), AZER4 15, SAUDI2 6 (one better).

